ces went full virtual this year but that  didn't stop companies from showing off  the latest in tech gadgets and  entertainment from across the world but  what does that mean  for the gamers among us well we've gone  ahead and gathered up a few of the most  exciting or interesting announcements  and we've got everything from giant 8k  tvs to rgb face masks with even more  coming soon so be sure to subscribe so  you don't miss out on that  now ces doesn't focus too much on actual  video games more on the tech that drives  them and the way we interact with our  entertainment systems but during sony's  stream it did show off some exciting  release dates for some upcoming titles  this includes kana bridge of spirits  releasing this march  solar ash coming june ghostwire tokyo  and stray  that's the adorable cat game we all fell  in love with e3 last year are both  dropping  this october and project atheia is  coming in january 2022.  however pragmata capcom's mysterious  weird astronaut game that we've not  heard a peep out of  since e3 2020 is in fact getting delayed  until 2023  so it'll be a while longer until we can  figure out what's going on with the  strange sky glitches and the android cat  that were teased  seven long months ago on the pc side  though there is some cool expanded  support for some current games with  rainbow six siege and overwatch being  added to the list of games that can make  use of nvidia's reflex tech  reflex reduces latency by combining  optimizations between both the gpu and  the games themselves  and while it's not a huge draw for fps  fans right now it's cool to see that  nvidia has its eyes on the horizon and  this is a system the company is keen to  support for a good while  rather than a gimmick or experiment that  gets hung out to dry  and there's exciting news for everyone  still feverishly trying to get their  hands on nvidia's latest generation of  graphics cards  during ces nvidia revealed its fourth  graphics card in the growing rtx 30  series line  the new 30 60 card is the cheapest in  the range  while still delivering some impressive  performance numbers although considering  that the 3060 ti was only released back  in december  it is a slightly strange offering many  of the rtx 30 cards are as rare as  rocking horse poop  and have been selling out in the blink  of an eye so it's good to see that  there's more powerful hardware coming  down the line  especially as this card is going to be  launching at 329 usd  and boasts twice the performance of the  old gtx 1060 which  is a big step in allowing more gamers to  make the most of all the lovely new ray  tracing and dlss options  available in recent games with 12  gigabytes of gddr6  over 3500 nvidia cudicores and clocking  in  at 1.78 gigahertz this is again  a lot of power for a really decent price  and also matches nvidia's aim for the  3060 to bring their new architecture  to every gamer and exciting news for  anyone who prefers their pc gaming on  the go  or just favors a slimmer form factor for  their machines  nvidia is bringing its 30 series gpus  into the next generation of laptops  these lappies are built on the latest  ampere architecture and 3rd gen max q  performance  and stress optimization technology which  will hopefully mean that you can pump  out higher frames per second without  your system's fans taking off  or your laptop setting fire to your  thighs laptops equipped with the 360 are  reported to allow for 90 fps gameplay  with ultra settings at 1080p  and these will be starting at 999 3070  laptops are said to be 1.5 faster than  the rtx 2070 gpu  and allow for 90 fps action with ultra  settings on many games at 1440p  obviously the price is a little ramped  up here at 1300  and lastly the 3080 equipped laptops  have 16 gigabytes of gddr6  and can push gameplay past 100 fps with  ultra settings  at 1440p as expected though these models  are going to set you back a few more  bucks  starting around 2 000 but it's not just  gamers that nvidia are trying to cater  to though stating that this performance  is for both work and play  with their studio laptop models and  whatever branded agencies you have  you'll surely have something to suit  your tastes as there are over  70 of these laptops launching later this  month and these of course come from all  the usual suspects like acer  asus rog and razer and speaking of the  mean green snake shape machine razer  showed off some  peculiar concepts during this year's ces  on top  of all the laptop announcements most  notable is an immersive gaming chair  with a  60 inch oled screen which i'm almost  certain will be the first step to us  becoming those floating chair humans  from wally there's also a smart  n95 face mask that not only protects you  and those around you but allows you to  apply  gamer rgb to your own face project  brooklyn is their concept what they're  calling a truly immersive gaming station  which comes complete with an  oled surround screen is built with  carbon fiber is covered in rgb lighting  and is designed around  a full cockpit experience i would say it  looks like an intense piece of kit but  i'm sitting here in front of three  computer monitors so i can't really  critique when it comes to gaming battle  station design but moving on to project  hazel razer's smart mask this is  something i am really quite  interested in despite it being in only a  conceptual stage  a surgical n95 made of clear plastic  featuring wireless charging  voice amplification rechargeable  ventilators uv sterilization  and again the ability to light up my  face in whatever colored lighting i want  honestly sign me up i must say though  that some of the reactions  are gold shout out to mr kepling's  comment on our youtube video  i could finally breathe in 60 fps  is absolutely fantastic although i think  we can all accept that masks aren't  going to go anywhere anytime soon so  it's pretty cool  to see razer applying some of its  ingenuity to them they've been providing  frontline workers with masks since the  pandemic started but if they're going to  start selling something that lets me  dress up my face as if i'm one of the  cyberpunk 2077 npcs then i really am  all for it there was also a big showing  on the monitor and tv front as well  which makes a lot of sense now that the  new generation of gpus from both amd and  nvidia are out in the wild and gamers  are getting their hands on the new  playstation 5  and xbox series x's naturally the best  way to see all those beautiful pixels in  buttery smooth frames are via  a nice shiny monitor or television asus  announced three  new gaming monitors the tough gaming  vg28uq  l1a the rog swift xg43  and the rg swift pg32uq all names that  are  really totally memorable and just roll  off the tongue  but as they feature hdmi 2.1 and 4k  support  they do at least seem to be good options  for console gaming as well  as being part of your pc battle station  if the big screen is more your bags  samsung  sony tcl and lg all got to showcase  their cutting edge tvs  everything from 99 inch screens and 8k  resolutions  across all of these offerings so you can  be sure your games will look the best  they can be  personally the part i get excited about  is that whenever all these super fancy  tvs get announced and their prices are  showing off later down the line  some older but still fantastic  televisions get reduced in price  so make sure you keep your eyes open for  some bargains shout out to the gamespot  deals twitter over the next few months  now that's all we've got time for in  this video but be sure to check out our  full ces coverage on gamespot.com to  read more about  everything you've seen here as well as a  few things we've missed  if you enjoyed the video click the like  button let us know what you're most  excited about in the comment section  below  and we will see you in the next one  [Music]  so  [Music]  you
 

